[{:db/id 17592186166726 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-45075cea-f15c-5084-914d-ebb143f8bab5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166494 :question/problem "Consider the binomial random variable $X\\sim B(7, 0.63).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing values in the cumulative distribution function table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X \\leq x)$ | $0.0009$ | $0.0123$ | $0.0701$ | $0.2341$ | $0.5134$ | $0.7987$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\displaystyle \\binom{n}{x} p^x (1-p)^{n-x}, \\qquad x=0,1,2,\\ldots,n.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $n=7$ and $p=0.63.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n- For $F(6),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 5)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =F(5)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =0.7987+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{6})(0.63)^{6}(1-0.63)^{7-6} \\\\  & =0.7987+7\\cdot (0.63)^{6}\\cdot (0.37)^{1} \\\\  & ≈0.9606.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Since $n=7,$ we have that $F(7) = P(X\\leq 7) = 1.$\n\nTherefore, our completed table looks as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X \\leq x)$ | $0.0009$ | $0.0123$ | $0.0701$ | $0.2341$ | $0.5134$ | $0.7987$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.9606}$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$ |" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166727 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c7cc6a15-4009-5db6-878e-1743f9fb14e2" "question-84b86fdf-72f2-5ecd-9ec1-a3a6650f805e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166495 :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(6, 0.67)$ given below, compute $P(X=2).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0013\\,$ | $\\,0.0170\\,$ | $\\,0.0969\\,$ | $\\,0.3130\\,$ | $\\,0.6422\\,$ | $\\,0.9095\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1\\})+P(X=2) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =F(1)+P(X=2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2) & =F(2)-F(1) \\\\  & =0.0969-0.0170 \\\\  & =0.0799\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166728 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-39452c92-9de3-5f42-bbde-2d7fa0b6b73d" "question-af275350-4175-5761-af0d-7b660329cfde"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166496 :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(6, 0.47)$ given below, compute $P(1 \\leq X \\lt 5).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0222\\,$ | $\\,0.1401\\,$ | $\\,0.4015\\,$ | $\\,0.7107\\,$ | $\\,0.9163\\,$ | $\\,0.9892\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(4) & =P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0\\})+P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 0)+P(1\\le X<5) \\\\  & =F(0)+P(1\\le X<5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X<5) & =F(4)-F(0) \\\\  & =0.9163-0.0222 \\\\  & =0.8941.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166729 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3dbd9a46-63be-542a-8056-c34929af9e15" "question-b6ff4041-b681-52c7-96bc-3e966d10e527"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166497 :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(7, 0.52)$ given below, compute $P(X \\geq 2).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0059\\,$ | $\\,0.0504\\,$ | $\\,0.1951\\,$ | $\\,0.4563\\,$ | $\\,0.7393\\,$ | $\\,0.9233\\,$ | $\\,0.9897\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X > a) = 1 - P(X\\leq a) = 1-F(a).\n$$\n\nNow, note that \n\n$$\nP(X \\geq 2) = P(X \\gt 1).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & =P(X>1) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =1-F(1) \\\\  & =1-0.0504 \\\\  & =0.9496.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167141 :question/problem "Consider the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.26).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing values in the cumulative distribution function table below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $\\,0.8144\\,$ | $\\,0.9569\\,$ | $\\,0.9944\\,$ | $\\,0.9997\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\\,x=0,1,2,…,n.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $n=6$ and $p=0.26.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =P(X\\le 0) \\\\  & =P(X=0) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{0})(0.26)^{0}(1-0.26)^{6-0} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (0.26)^{0}\\cdot (0.74)^{6} \\\\  & ≈0.1642.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{0})(0.26)^{0}(1-0.26)^{6-0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{1})(0.26)^{1}(1-0.26)^{6-1} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (0.26)^{0}\\cdot (0.74)^{6}+6\\cdot (0.26)^{1}\\cdot (0.74)^{5} \\\\  & ≈0.5104.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163919 :answer-field/correct "answer-d39bc26a-bf73-5514-8ace-4df9549e3b22" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d39bc26a-bf73-5514-8ace-4df9549e3b22"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d39bc26a-bf73-5514-8ace-4df9549e3b22" :answer/id #uuid "d39bc26a-bf73-5514-8ace-4df9549e3b22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1642" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163920 :answer-field/correct "answer-844474bb-952f-5653-9c05-58decf91ec4d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-844474bb-952f-5653-9c05-58decf91ec4d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-844474bb-952f-5653-9c05-58decf91ec4d" :answer/id #uuid "844474bb-952f-5653-9c05-58decf91ec4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5104" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-45075cea-f15c-5084-914d-ebb143f8bab5" :question/id #uuid "45075cea-f15c-5084-914d-ebb143f8bab5" :question/math-academy-id "q-224505" :question/problem "Consider the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.65).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing value in the cumulative distribution function table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $0.0018$ | $0.0223$ | $0.1174$ | $0.3529$ | $0.6809$ | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\\,x=0,1,2,…,n.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $n=6$ and $p=0.65.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing element of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =0.6809+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{5})(0.65)^{5}(1-0.65)^{6-5} \\\\  & =0.6809+6\\cdot (0.65)^{5}\\cdot (0.35)^{1} \\\\  & ≈0.9246.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dd714c02-0a09-5253-9229-c78cde01f445"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dd714c02-0a09-5253-9229-c78cde01f445" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd714c02-0a09-5253-9229-c78cde01f445" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-62630e8d-d2db-5fcf-a9ee-7b86c738a8c0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-62630e8d-d2db-5fcf-a9ee-7b86c738a8c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62630e8d-d2db-5fcf-a9ee-7b86c738a8c0" :answer/id #uuid "62630e8d-d2db-5fcf-a9ee-7b86c738a8c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9246" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c7cc6a15-4009-5db6-878e-1743f9fb14e2" :question/id #uuid "c7cc6a15-4009-5db6-878e-1743f9fb14e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-224526" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.48)$ given below, compute $P(X=3).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0198\\,$ | $\\,0.1293\\,$ | $\\,0.3820\\,$ | $\\,0.6930\\,$ | $\\,0.9083\\,$ | $\\,0.9878\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(X=3)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(3) & =P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X=3) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(X=3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =F(3)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.6930-0.3820 \\\\  & =0.3110.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1bd2bd7d-81b6-570e-8fdd-b4fa401ea4d8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1bd2bd7d-81b6-570e-8fdd-b4fa401ea4d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd2bd7d-81b6-570e-8fdd-b4fa401ea4d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e263b34c-fdc3-56a1-821a-cd91cd1eecfa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e263b34c-fdc3-56a1-821a-cd91cd1eecfa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e263b34c-fdc3-56a1-821a-cd91cd1eecfa" :answer/id #uuid "e263b34c-fdc3-56a1-821a-cd91cd1eecfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3110" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-84b86fdf-72f2-5ecd-9ec1-a3a6650f805e" :question/id #uuid "84b86fdf-72f2-5ecd-9ec1-a3a6650f805e" :question/math-academy-id "q-224517" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(7,0.85)$ given below, compute $P(X<5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0000\\,$ | $\\,0.0001\\,$ | $\\,0.0012\\,$ | $\\,0.0121\\,$ | $\\,0.0738\\,$ | $\\,0.2834\\,$ | $\\,0.6794\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =F(4) \\\\  & =0.0738.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a166156c-a351-5495-9912-8c241a9caedf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a166156c-a351-5495-9912-8c241a9caedf" :answer-field/id #uuid "a166156c-a351-5495-9912-8c241a9caedf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d35be4b5-858a-50e5-916c-a8c257d81867" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d35be4b5-858a-50e5-916c-a8c257d81867" "answer-4d21eaac-b64d-59c5-a232-eec231b01fdd" "answer-f232fefc-778d-57b7-9c36-9f38d8b9078a" "answer-dac293d3-2b8c-5f02-8569-0ff33e3f1998" "answer-45c1d3ae-7aea-5878-b0b0-750018287438"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d35be4b5-858a-50e5-916c-a8c257d81867" :answer/id #uuid "d35be4b5-858a-50e5-916c-a8c257d81867" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0738" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d21eaac-b64d-59c5-a232-eec231b01fdd" :answer/id #uuid "4d21eaac-b64d-59c5-a232-eec231b01fdd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0872" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f232fefc-778d-57b7-9c36-9f38d8b9078a" :answer/id #uuid "f232fefc-778d-57b7-9c36-9f38d8b9078a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2096" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dac293d3-2b8c-5f02-8569-0ff33e3f1998" :answer/id #uuid "dac293d3-2b8c-5f02-8569-0ff33e3f1998" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2834" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45c1d3ae-7aea-5878-b0b0-750018287438" :answer/id #uuid "45c1d3ae-7aea-5878-b0b0-750018287438" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6794" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-39452c92-9de3-5f42-bbde-2d7fa0b6b73d" :question/id #uuid "39452c92-9de3-5f42-bbde-2d7fa0b6b73d" :question/math-academy-id "q-225125" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.8)$ given below, compute $P(1\\le X\\le 6).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0001\\,$ | $\\,0.0016\\,$ | $\\,0.0170\\,$ | $\\,0.0989\\,$ | $\\,0.3446\\,$ | $\\,0.7379\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0\\})+P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 0)+P(1\\le X\\le 6) \\\\  & =F(0)+P(1\\le X\\le 6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X\\le 6) & =F(6)-F(0) \\\\  & =1.0000-0.0001 \\\\  & =0.9999.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f954b4ca-ba90-55e4-8907-f07c9675da77"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f954b4ca-ba90-55e4-8907-f07c9675da77" :answer-field/id #uuid "f954b4ca-ba90-55e4-8907-f07c9675da77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c93d79d2-a698-5d23-83bc-eaa0004f68c7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-630e58a3-661e-52d8-a8d1-903e9b5e6179" "answer-363c6137-dca5-587b-9559-70490db1b35a" "answer-0ade8b6c-624a-50a4-bad2-15e70c431679" "answer-3b049551-1d9e-51e1-a8e6-dd6c16d4ea52" "answer-c93d79d2-a698-5d23-83bc-eaa0004f68c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-630e58a3-661e-52d8-a8d1-903e9b5e6179" :answer/id #uuid "630e58a3-661e-52d8-a8d1-903e9b5e6179" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0001" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-363c6137-dca5-587b-9559-70490db1b35a" :answer/id #uuid "363c6137-dca5-587b-9559-70490db1b35a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0989" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ade8b6c-624a-50a4-bad2-15e70c431679" :answer/id #uuid "0ade8b6c-624a-50a4-bad2-15e70c431679" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9011" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b049551-1d9e-51e1-a8e6-dd6c16d4ea52" :answer/id #uuid "3b049551-1d9e-51e1-a8e6-dd6c16d4ea52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9984" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c93d79d2-a698-5d23-83bc-eaa0004f68c7" :answer/id #uuid "c93d79d2-a698-5d23-83bc-eaa0004f68c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9999" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-af275350-4175-5761-af0d-7b660329cfde" :question/id #uuid "af275350-4175-5761-af0d-7b660329cfde" :question/math-academy-id "q-225123" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(5,0.63)$ given below, compute $P(2<X\\le 5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0069\\,$ | $\\,0.0660\\,$ | $\\,0.2670\\,$ | $\\,0.6093\\,$ | $\\,0.9008\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(2<X\\le 5)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(2<X\\le 5) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(2<X\\le 5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X\\le 5) & =F(5)-F(2) \\\\  & =1.0000-0.2670 \\\\  & =0.7330.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e53b86c5-f2cb-5dad-8677-36c6c80c81f6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e53b86c5-f2cb-5dad-8677-36c6c80c81f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "e53b86c5-f2cb-5dad-8677-36c6c80c81f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1686d601-47e1-567a-99f3-65018bc5b85f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1686d601-47e1-567a-99f3-65018bc5b85f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1686d601-47e1-567a-99f3-65018bc5b85f" :answer/id #uuid "1686d601-47e1-567a-99f3-65018bc5b85f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7330" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3dbd9a46-63be-542a-8056-c34929af9e15" :question/id #uuid "3dbd9a46-63be-542a-8056-c34929af9e15" :question/math-academy-id "q-225192" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(7,0.48)$ given below, compute $P(X>5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0103\\,$ | $\\,0.0767\\,$ | $\\,0.2607\\,$ | $\\,0.5437\\,$ | $\\,0.8049\\,$ | $\\,0.9496\\,$ | $\\,0.9941\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(X>5)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>5) & =1-P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =1-F(5) \\\\  & =1-0.9496 \\\\  & =0.0504.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5d59258b-b2f8-5954-823d-22bfd5f84b58"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5d59258b-b2f8-5954-823d-22bfd5f84b58" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d59258b-b2f8-5954-823d-22bfd5f84b58" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-08b0954c-0b0f-5d90-bc97-b401944c0b15" :answer-field/choices ["answer-08b0954c-0b0f-5d90-bc97-b401944c0b15"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08b0954c-0b0f-5d90-bc97-b401944c0b15" :answer/id #uuid "08b0954c-0b0f-5d90-bc97-b401944c0b15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0504" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b6ff4041-b681-52c7-96bc-3e966d10e527" :question/id #uuid "b6ff4041-b681-52c7-96bc-3e966d10e527" :question/math-academy-id "q-225190" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(5,0.79)$ given below, compute $P(X>3).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0004\\,$ | $\\,0.0081\\,$ | $\\,0.0659\\,$ | $\\,0.2833\\,$ | $\\,0.6923\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3) & =1-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =1-F(3) \\\\  & =1-0.2833 \\\\  & =0.7167.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f5be0410-2431-593a-bcce-244299805303"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f5be0410-2431-593a-bcce-244299805303" :answer-field/id #uuid "f5be0410-2431-593a-bcce-244299805303" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-65f07f98-a8b9-5622-9b27-3d53b4b91fe2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f23fa1b7-310e-5e39-a994-088b046f6326" "answer-4368e1e2-68d4-5d71-8fdb-de90614b84c6" "answer-557c159a-30a2-562f-a119-f39d2d4ff550" "answer-65f07f98-a8b9-5622-9b27-3d53b4b91fe2" "answer-aaaac3c2-cb51-55eb-b7b3-6b277435e640"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f23fa1b7-310e-5e39-a994-088b046f6326" :answer/id #uuid "f23fa1b7-310e-5e39-a994-088b046f6326" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2833" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4368e1e2-68d4-5d71-8fdb-de90614b84c6" :answer/id #uuid "4368e1e2-68d4-5d71-8fdb-de90614b84c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3077" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-557c159a-30a2-562f-a119-f39d2d4ff550" :answer/id #uuid "557c159a-30a2-562f-a119-f39d2d4ff550" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6923" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65f07f98-a8b9-5622-9b27-3d53b4b91fe2" :answer/id #uuid "65f07f98-a8b9-5622-9b27-3d53b4b91fe2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7167" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aaaac3c2-cb51-55eb-b7b3-6b277435e640" :answer/id #uuid "aaaac3c2-cb51-55eb-b7b3-6b277435e640" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9341" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186168156 :tutorial/content "When performing certain types of statistical tests (e.g., hypothesis testing), we often need to use standard cumulative distribution function (CDF) tables to carry out the test. \n\nIn this lesson, we'll learn how to construct CDF tables for the binomial distribution and use them to calculate probabilities. \n\nFirst, recall that the probability mass function of the binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\binom{n}{x} \\, p^x (1-p)^{n-x}, \\qquad x=0,1,2,\\ldots, n\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success.\n\nAlso, recall that the CDF of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's compute the value of $F(x)$ for the distribution $B(5,0.37)$ at $x=0$ and $x=1.$  \n\nTo do that, we use the definition of the cumulative distribution function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =P(X\\le 0) \\\\  & =P(X=0) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{0})(0.37)^{0}(1-0.37)^{5-0} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (0.37)^{0}\\cdot (0.63)^{5} \\\\  & ≈0.0992 \\\\ F(1) & =P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{0})(0.37)^{0}(1-0.37)^{5-0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{1})(0.37)^{1}(1-0.37)^{5-1} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (0.37)^{0}\\cdot (0.63)^{5}+5\\cdot (0.37)^{1}\\cdot (0.63)^{4} \\\\  & ≈0.3907.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe CDF data is usually presented as a table. If we were to continue this process and calculate $F(2), F(3), F(4),$ and $F(5),$ our table would look as follows:\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,\\bbox[gainsboro, 3pt]{\\color{blue}0.0992}\\,$ | $\\,\\bbox[gainsboro, 3pt]{\\color{blue}0.3907}\\,$ | $\\,0.7330\\,$ | $\\,0.9340\\,$ | $\\,0.9931\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\nNote the following:\n\n- $F(x)$ is an increasing function.\n\n- Since $n$ is the largest possible value of the binomial distribution, we have $F(n) = 1.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167034 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
